## Midterm: Binary Tree Preorder Traversal
**Difficulty**: Easy

**Problem Statement**
Given the root of a binary tree, return its preorder traversal (root, left, right) of node values, space-separated on one line. If the tree is empty, print an empty line.

**Input Format**
A single line containing the level-order serialization of the tree (see the "Tree input convention" at the top of this file). Tokens are space-separated; `null` denotes an absent node.

**Output Format**
A single line with the preorder traversal of the node values, separated by single spaces. Print an empty line if the tree is empty.

**Constraints**
- `0 <= number of nodes <= 100000`
- `-10^9 <= Node.val <= 10^9`
- The intended solution runs in `O(N)` time and `O(H)` auxiliary space, where `H` is the tree height. Hidden tests include deeply skewed trees (`H ≈ N`), so recursion without tail elimination may stack-overflow — an explicit stack or careful recursion is expected.

**Sample Input 0**
```
1 null 2 3
```

**Sample Output 0**
```
1 2 3
```

**Sample Explanation 0**
The tree has root `1` with no left child and right child `2`, whose left child is `3`. Preorder visits root → left → right: visit `1`, then recurse right into `2`, visit `2`, then recurse left into `3`, visit `3`. Final order: `1 2 3`.

**Sample Input 1**
```

```

**Sample Output 1**
```

```

**Sample Explanation 1**
The input line is empty, so the tree has no nodes. The preorder traversal is also empty.

**Sample Input 2**
```
1
```

**Sample Output 2**
```
1
```

**Sample Input 3**
```
1 2 3 4 5 6 7
```

**Sample Output 3**
```
1 2 4 5 3 6 7
```

**Sample Input 4**
```
5 3 8 1 4 7 9
```

**Sample Output 4**
```
5 3 1 4 8 7 9
```

**Sample Input 5**
```
1 2 null 3 null 4
```

**Sample Output 5**
```
1 2 3 4
```

**Sample Input 6**
```
1 null 2 null 3 null 4
```

**Sample Output 6**
```
1 2 3 4
```

**Sample Input 7**
```
10 5 15 null null 12 20
```

**Sample Output 7**
```
10 5 15 12 20
```

**Sample Input 8**
```
-1 -2 -3
```

**Sample Output 8**
```
-1 -2 -3
```

**Sample Input 9**
```
7 3 9 1 5 8 10
```

**Sample Output 9**
```
7 3 1 5 9 8 10
```

**Tags**
Binary Tree, DFS, Recursion

**Boilerplate (C++14)** — NOT parsed by the automator. Paste into HackerRank admin **Head Code / Body / Tail Code** slots after upload.

Head Code:
```cpp
#include <bits/stdc++.h>
using namespace std;

struct TreeNode {
    int val;
    TreeNode* left;
    TreeNode* right;
    TreeNode(int v) : val(v), left(nullptr), right(nullptr) {}
};

static TreeNode* buildTree(const string& line) {
    vector<string> toks;
    {
        stringstream ss(line);
        string t;
        while (ss >> t) toks.push_back(t);
    }
    if (toks.empty() || toks[0] == "null") return nullptr;
    TreeNode* root = new TreeNode(stoi(toks[0]));
    queue<TreeNode*> q;
    q.push(root);
    size_t i = 1;
    while (!q.empty() && i < toks.size()) {
        TreeNode* node = q.front(); q.pop();
        if (i < toks.size()) {
            if (toks[i] != "null") {
                node->left = new TreeNode(stoi(toks[i]));
                q.push(node->left);
            }
            ++i;
        }
        if (i < toks.size()) {
            if (toks[i] != "null") {
                node->right = new TreeNode(stoi(toks[i]));
                q.push(node->right);
            }
            ++i;
        }
    }
    return root;
}
```

Solution Template (the user writes only this):
